RetViM release maintained by Khamir Desai.

The accompanying paper lists Khamir Desai, Mayuri A. Mehta, and
Sree Saicharan Vadapalli. See CITATION.cff for scholarly attribution.

This package uses timm (Apache-2.0), PyTorch and torchvision (BSD-style)
as dependencies. Their licenses remain applicable to those dependencies.

The Mamba selective-state-space recurrence follows the method of Gu and Dao
and was checked against the official Mamba selective_scan_ref equations:
https://github.com/state-spaces/mamba
https://arxiv.org/abs/2312.00752
Mamba's upstream implementation is Apache-2.0 licensed. This release uses
an independently written PyTorch reference path; it does not ship CUDA kernels.
